description: Rook core rules — constitution, invariants, and workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root before making changes — it is the
authoritative guide (constitution, architecture map, dev workflow, danger
zones). The non-negotiables, in brief:

- Rook prices nothing: no code may set, target, or predict an asset price.
  The house mover stays directional-only, capped (`mover.capC`), and
  decaying with organic volume.
- Metrics come from market activity only (trades, flow, holdings) — never
  from sporting prediction. Standings are display + disclosed settlement
  rule, never a pricing input.
- Equal stacks; money never buys position. Play-money only; no cash-out.
- All market mutations go through `executeUserTrade` — never write
  `assets.supply`, `holdings`, or `balances` directly. `trades` is
  append-only; house trades are flagged and logged.
- Tunables live in the versioned `config` table; `loadConfig` folds ALL
  effective rows in order — never hardcode a tunable, never break the fold.
- `packages/engine` stays pure and deterministic: no I/O, no `Date.now()`,
  no unseeded randomness. Timestamps are injected as `now: Date` params.
- Chess vocabulary in status/identity only; Buy/Sell stay plain finance
  verbs. Dark UI, no casino green.
- Product docs: `docs/v1-product-spec.md`, `docs/rook-breakdown.md`,
  `docs/phase0-results.md`.

Workflow: Postgres via `docker compose up -d` (:5455) → `npm run -w
@rook/db migrate` → `npm test` (engine then core; core is serial,
DB-backed). CI also typechecks each package and builds the web app.
